From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] permit bounded STA social-channel ROC beside monitor

0015 revision captured 316 raw monitor frames across six synchronous slots,
while ordinary Wi-Fi stayed associated and gateway responses were 47/48,
then 3/3 after the experiment. The existing HDD STA+MON check rejects all
ROC requests before reaching normal scan scheduling. Under default-off
0009 only, allow <=200ms ROC on 6/44/149 from the associated STA. All normal
regulatory, firmware, policy manager and scan scheduling still apply. Other
interfaces, frequencies and durations retain the original rejection.
No monitor channel retune, RAW data TX or automatic slot loop is added.

diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
  *
  */
 
+#include "marionette_sta_monitor.h"
 #include "marionette_awdl_rx_diagnostics.h"
 #include "osif_sync.h"
 #include <wlan_hdd_includes.h>
@@ -179,8 +180,19 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (policy_mgr_is_sta_mon_concurrency(hdd_ctx->psoc))
-		return -EINVAL;
+	if (policy_mgr_is_sta_mon_concurrency(hdd_ctx->psoc)) {
+		/* Keep the normal scheduling/regulatory path, permitting only
+		 * explicitly gated short AWDL social-channel receive dwells. */
+		if (!marionette_sta_monitor_enabled() ||
+		    adapter->device_mode != QDF_STA_MODE ||
+		    !hdd_cm_is_vdev_associated(adapter) || !chan ||
+		    !duration || duration > 200 ||
+		    (chan->center_freq != 2437 && chan->center_freq != 5220 &&
+		     chan->center_freq != 5745))
+			return -EINVAL;
+		hdd_info("MARIONETTE_STA_MON_ROC freq=%u duration=%u",
+			 chan->center_freq, duration);
+	}
 
 	if (wlan_hdd_validate_vdev_id(adapter->vdev_id))
 		return -EINVAL;
